dot/issues/111568","id":3402458247,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KzWSH","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T15:36:00Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T15:36:00Z","body":"I've used both Mathematica and Excel to make polynomial approximations. But Mathematica's `NonlinearModelFit` can sometimes be useful as well, as you get to specify the output function and parameters that you want fitted to the source data. I expect this wouldn't be useful for this case, though, so probably a basic polynomial regression is the best bet?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3402458247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3418724595","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111568#issuecomment-3418724595","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111568","id":3418724595,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LxZjz","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-18T18:26:12Z","updated_at":"2025-10-18T18:26:12Z","body":"@LiveTrower Can you post the buffer of floats you want us to curve fit?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3418724595/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3419073344","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111568#issuecomment-3419073344","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111568","id":3419073344,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LyutA","user":{"login":"LiveTrower","id":48926464,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OTI2NDY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48926464?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower","html_url":"https://github.com/LiveTrower","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-19T00:00:11Z","updated_at":"2025-10-19T00:00:11Z","body":"> @LiveTrower Can you post the buffer of floats you want us to curve fit?\r\n\r\nI don't know if this is what you want, but I'm leaving you a zip file with a Python script to read the DFG LUT and extract the values from the blue channel, which is where the Sheen LUT is located.\r\n\r\n[dds_values.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22987653/dds_values.zip)\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3419073344/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3425034925","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111568#issuecomment-3425034925","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111568","id":3425034925,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MJeKt","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T07:00:31Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T08:28:56Z","body":"@LiveTrower Here's an CHOP-coded approximation https://github.com/fire/godot-sheen-look-up-table\r\n\r\nI'm not sure how low the mean error we should attempt, feel free to experiment. \r\n\r\nSuggest playing with the degree variable. https://github.com/fire/godot-sheen-look-up-table/blob/26b7afd775177f1dbbd2956d99af2da2b04307b7/main.py#L21\r\n\r\nEdited:\r\n\r\nUpdated the readme. Was previously describing a rational function, but moved back to polynomial.\r\n\r\nEdited:\r\n\r\nInteresting results at deg 0, deg 1, deg 4, and deg 8.\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\ndds_values> uv run python .\\main.py\r\nApproximated analytical expression for the sheen LUT:\r\n0.0664957578919711\r\nMean Squared Error: 0.01711980566830958\r\ndds_values> uv run python .\\main.py\r\nApproximated analytical expression for the sheen LUT:\r\n-0.25030720970041*cos_theta + 0.180297312733505*r + 0.101500706375423\r\nMean Squared Error: 0.009064854351581322\r\ngodot-sheen-look-up-table> uv run python .\\main.py\r\nApproximated analytical expression for the sheen LUT:\r\n-2.8418752634654*cos_theta**4 - 0.0752492803140749*cos_theta**3*r + 5.79787608128554*cos_theta**3 + 2.48562696566899*cos_theta**2*r**2 - 1.00253162077076*cos_theta**2*r - 3.65901503993457*cos_theta**2 + 0.276146452617512*cos_theta*r**3 - 3.8030419846424*cos_theta*r**2 + 1.42331784042998*cos_theta*r + 0.658695894178778*cos_theta - 0.823548193452199*r**4 + 1.35743804092077*r**3 + 0.430920102235383*r**2 - 0.224877093447145*r + 0.0132743926195602\r\nMean Squared Error: 0.002395069535344717\r\ndds_values> uv run python .\\main.py\r\nApproximated analytical expression for the sheen LUT:\r\n-557.091779271558*cos_theta**8 + 464.017389846217*cos_theta**7*r + 2152.1266164332*cos_theta**7 - 230.321684192249*cos_theta**6*r**2 - 1525.96376250796*cos_theta**6*r - 3384.23333420742*cos_theta**6 + 2.86174085877387*cos_theta**5*r**3 + 744.890840615195*cos_theta**5*r**2 + 1932.42802940127*cos_theta**5*r + 2787.74835270357*cos_theta**5 + 104.289164776309*cos_theta**4*r**4 - 194.098783820854*cos_theta**4*r**3 - 825.798219330147*cos_theta**4*r**2 - 1189.47390170691*cos_theta**4*r - 1289.70446461101*cos_theta**4 + 16.4307961138826*cos_theta**3*r**5 - 264.236227330607*cos_theta**3*r**4 + 435.698733067964*cos_theta**3*r**3 + 330.115180358558*cos_theta**3*r**2 + 377.760815347863*cos_theta**3*r + 333.246911023428*cos_theta**3 - 33.7673457364751*cos_theta**2*r**6 + 56.2723698949418*cos_theta**2*r**5 + 148.016374822698*cos_theta**2*r**4 - 297.359389044023*cos_theta**2*r**3 - 3.59259176216401*cos_theta**2*r**2 - 64.9201817967158*cos_theta**2*r - 44.5916577589042*cos_theta**2 - 12.0589143469186*cos_theta*r**7 + 79.3217215327783*cos_theta*r**6 - 133.214050066957*cos_theta*r**5 + 45.9217563239256*cos_theta*r**4 + 45.1941989068905*cos_theta*r**3 - 14.9524287804133*cos_theta*r**2 + 6.30200063105549*cos_theta*r + 2.44540720268555*cos_theta + 8.53860911397782*r**8 - 24.68454951197*r**7 + 15.367948662591*r**6 + 11.3701055151527*r**5 - 13.5672939003094*r**4 + 2.94229103229011*r**3 + 0.453115385148636*r**2 - 0.128715903958555*r - 0.00103032751274113\r\nMean Squared Error: 0.0009670587699536178\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3425034925/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized"